 FILE ASSEMBLY, VERIFICATION AND VALIDATION                       2525 1451   16
 Coordinator: A. Trkov                                            2525 1451   17
                                                                  2525 1451   18
 The file integrity and internal consistency with respect         2525 1451   19
 to format requirements was checked with the ENDF Utility         2525 1451   20
 codes and ENDF Pre-Processing codes. Processability was          2525 1451   21
 checked by generating and ACE file for Monte Carlo               2525 1451   22
 calculations and a multigroup file in MATXS format for           2525 1451   23
 deterministic calculations. The plots produced by the heatr      2525 1451   24
 and acer modules of NJOY were inspected. Comparison plots        2525 1451   25
 were made with ENDF/B-VII.0 data. Furthermore, comparison        2525 1451   26
 plots with the ENDVER package were made against selected         2525 1451   27
 experimental data from the EXFOR database.                       2525 1451   28
                                                                  2525 1451   29
 Integral validation was performed by comparing the thermal       2525 1451   30
 capture cross section Sig0 and ratio Q0 of the resonance         2525 1451   31
 integrals and the thermal cross section values from the          2525 1451   32
 IUPAC database for neutron activation analysis                   2525 1451   33
        IUPAC       This work   ENDF/B-VII.0                      2525 1451   34
 Sig0   13.19-+0.6% 13.27-+1.1% 13.42                             2525 1451   35
 Q0     1.053-+3.0% 0.998-+3.6% 0.867                             2525 1451   36
                                                                  2525 1451   37
 More extensive testing of the cross sections in the resonance    2525 1451   38
 region was done by modelling the Grenoble lead-slowing-down      2525 1451   39
 benchmark (Perrot et al. NSE 144, 2003, p.p.142-156), which      2525 1451   40
 showed excellent agreement of the calculated capture reaction    2525 1451   41
 rate with the measurement. The results explain the improvement   2525 1451   42
 in the Q0 value stated in the previous paragraph.                2525 1451   43
                                                                  2525 1451   44
 Cross sections in the fast energy range were probed by           2525 1451   45
 modelling the Oktavian benchmark from the SINBAD database, in    2525 1451   46
 which the leakage spectrum from a manganese sphere with a 14-MeV 2525 1451   47
 D-T source was measured. The results confirm good performance of 2525 1451   48
 the data, which is at least as good as any competing evaluation. 2525 1451   49
                                                                  2525 1451   50
 Detailed results will be presented in a separate report.         2525 1451   51
                                                                  2525 1451   52
 FAST ENERGY REGION                                               2525 1451   53
 Authors: R. Capote, E. Soukhovitskii, A. Trkov,                  2525 1451   54
          A. Milocco, M. Herman                                   2525 1451   55
                                                                  2525 1451   56
 CROSS-SECTION EVALUATION PROCEDURE                               2525 1451   57
                                                                  2525 1451   58
 Adopted procedure is based on careful theoretical                2525 1451   59
 analysis utilizing available experimental data and               2525 1451   60
 nuclear reaction model calculations.                             2525 1451   61
                                                                  2525 1451   62
 Available experimental data were interpreted  using              2525 1451   63
 nuclear reaction model code EMPIRE-3 by M. Herman                2525 1451   64
 et al [EMP]. This code integrates into a single                  2525 1451   65
 system a number of important modules and features:               2525 1451   66
                                                                  2525 1451   67
 - Spherical and deformed Optical Model including                 2525 1451   68
   coupled-channels (ECIS06 by J. Raynal)                         2525 1451   69
 - Hauser-Feshbach statistical model including                    2525 1451   70
   HRTW width fluctuation correction                              2525 1451   71
 - Quantum-mechanical MSD TUL model (codes ORION &                2525 1451   72
   TRISTAN by H. Lenske), and MSC NVWY model                      2525 1451   73
 - Exciton model with angular momentum coupling                   2525 1451   74
   (code DEGAS by E. Betak and P. Oblozinsky) that                2525 1451   75
   represents a good approximation to the DSD model               2525 1451   76
 - Exciton model with Iwamoto-Harada cluster                      2525 1451   77
   emission and Kalbach systematic angular distr.                 2525 1451   78
   (code PCROSS by R.Capote et al)                                2525 1451   79
 - Complete gamma-ray cascade after emission of                   2525 1451   80
   each particle, including realistic treatment of                2525 1451   81
   discrete transitions                                           2525 1451   82
 - Access to OM segment of the RIPL library [RIPL]                2525 1451   83
 - Built-in input parameter files, such as masses,                2525 1451   84
   level density, discrete levels, fission barriers               2525 1451   85
   and gamma strength functions based on the RIPL                 2525 1451   86
   library [RIPL]                                                 2525 1451   87
 - Automatic retrieval of experimental data from the              2525 1451   88
   EXFOR/CSISRS library                                           2525 1451   89
 - ENDF-6 formatting (code EMPEND by A. Trkov)                    2525 1451   90
   coupled to graphical presentation capabilities                 2525 1451   91
   (code ZVView by V. Zerkin) through the chain of                2525 1451   92
   PrePro codes by R. Cullen                                      2525 1451   93
 - Checking codes (CHECKR, FIZCON, PSYCHE)                        2525 1451   94
 - Support for NJOY                                               2525 1451   95
                                                                  2525 1451   96
