                                                                  2525 1451  502
Resonance parameter covariance was generated in the resolved      2525 1451  503
energy region (1.0-5 eV to 125 keV) with the computer code SAMMY  2525 1451  504
at ORNL. Experimental data and uncertainties were used to generate2525 1451  505
covariance data. SAMMY covariance information was converted in    2525 1451  506
the ENDF FILE32 representation. The covariance information was    2525 1451  507
processed with the PUFF-IV code.                                  2525 1451  508
                                                                  2525 1451  509
More information about the evaluation can be found in a paper by  2525 1451  510
Derrien et al. published in Physor08                              2525 1451  511
                                                                  2525 1451  512
******************************************************************2525 1451  513
ORNL November 2009 (H. Derrien, D. Wiarda)                        2525 1451  514
******************************************************************2525 1451  515
                                                                  2525 1451  516
Only the Resonance Parameter Covariance file(RPCM) was given in   2525 1451  517
ORNL 2007-2008 evaluation.  The uncertainties on the group        2525 1451  518
capture cross sections calculated from this RPCM were about 0.8%  2525 1451  519
at thermal energies and about 0.6-1.3% in the high energy groups  2525 1451  520
The uncertainties in the high energy ranges are obviously too     2525 1451  521
small, compared to those in the table above, as it was pointed out2525 1451  522
by P. Oblozinsky and C. Mattoon(2009)                             2525 1451  523
The RPCM was recalculated and a new file 32 was created           2525 1451  524
containing the uncertainties and covariances of the parameters    2525 1451  525
generated only from the stastistical uncertainties of the         2525 1451  526
experimental data base. The systematic uncertainties were         2525 1451  527
estimated from results obtained in the SAMMY analysis of the      2525 1451  528
experimental data base, from some information found in the        2525 1451  529
publications, and from discussion with some authors.  The cross   2525 1451  530
section covariance files 33001, 33002, and 33102 were then        2525 1451  531
obtained. The new ENDF file, processed by PUFF-IV, gave group     2525 1451  532
cross section uncertainties varying from 0.8% at 0.0253 eV to     2525 1451  533
7.4% at 10 eV, when the previous evaluations(ORNL and BNL) gave   2525 1451  534
a constant value of 0.8% below 10 eV. The calculated capture      2525 1451  535
cross section at 10 eV is about 0.5 b. The capture cross section  2525 1451  536
has been measured by Widder in the energy range 0.01 eV to 10 eV  2525 1451  537
with 4.2%, 1.9%, 5% accuracy at energies 0.01 eV, 0.0253 eV,10 eV 2525 1451  538
respectively, close to the values given in the present work.      2525 1451  539
